course: dictionary
lesson: 5494
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Laundry» is one of them. In «Setting the table and folding laundry are small jobs that save time for everyone», laundry means the clothes, sheets and towels that need washing or have just been washed.
explain: In «Laundry means sorting colours, reading labels and choosing the right temperature», laundry means the job of washing clothes. You cannot fold a job, so the clues tell you the meaning has changed. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Laundry can also mean a room or a business where clothes are washed. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the word. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Laundry is a noun, and it has no plural: you say some laundry, not two laundrys.
fact: «Laundry» means clothes, sheets and towels that need washing or have just been washed.
fact: «Laundry» also means the job of washing them, as in «do the laundry».
fact: A laundry is a room or a business where clothes are washed, and its plural is laundries.
fact: Laundry detergent pods are poisonous: never touch or eat them, and keep them away from small children.
exercise: «Setting the table and folding laundry are small jobs that save time for everyone.» What does laundry mean here? | *Clothes, sheets and towels that need washing or have just been washed | A pile of old newspapers | A room where clothes are washed | A shop that sells soap
exercise: «Laundry means sorting colours, reading labels and choosing the right temperature.» What does laundry mean here? | A room with washing machines | A washing line in the garden | Clothes that need washing | *The job of washing clothes
exercise: Ella takes the sheets to the local laundry to be washed. Where does she go? | A school hall | *A place where clothes are washed | A park with a lake | A shop selling shoes
test: Dad says, «I have done the laundry, so the basket is empty.» What does laundry mean? | A business that sells soap | *The job of washing clothes | A room where clothes are washed | Clothes that need washing
test: Why must you never touch or eat laundry detergent pods? | *They are poisonous and can cause burns and breathing problems | They make your hair curly | They are only for washing dogs | They are sweets for a treat
exam: Sam says his laundry is too big for the basket. What does laundry mean here? | A business that sells soap | A room where clothes are washed | The job of washing clothes | *Clothes that need washing or have just been washed
